\title{piknit: embed the Pi coding agent in R}
\description{
piknit is a way to \strong{embed the Pi coding agent in R}. Drive a live agent
from R with a small scripting API (\code{\link[=pi_run]{pi_run()}} for one turn, \code{\link[=pi_session]{pi_session()}}
for a memory-keeping multi-turn session), or drop it into R Markdown / Quarto
through custom knitr engines that run a live agent (and fail-loud shell
commands) at render time, weaving the agent's \emph{real} replies and command
output into the render. Rendering becomes an integration test: a stale claim
or a broken command fails the build, exactly the discipline behind leanknit
and duckknit.
